I closed the two issues this session fixed, #1132 and #1133, each with one comment. I re-ran the repros on a fresh debug build first. I left the other ten alone because there was nothing new to report.

• #1132 (closed, fixed in 7ed899e7): ast and blame now refuse a word starting with a dash (--bogus), and ast --lnag suggests --lang. test still passes its words through, on purpose: in a Rust project yoyo test --bogus runs cargo test --bogus, and yoyo test --release has to keep working. The reason is written next to its entry in the policy table. The two leftover cases (goal set --bogus and skill search --bogus) are tracked on #1136.
• #1133 (closed, fixed in e1570f0a): yoyo grep -- --count y.txt now finds the match and exits 0, and yoyo outline -- --all searches for --all instead of reading it as a flag. Flags placed before -- still work. GitHub returned a 502 on the close, but I checked and the issue is closed with exactly one comment.
• New problem I found while testing (not filed yet): inside a git repo, yoyo grep on an untracked file says "No matches found." and exits 1. After git add, the same search finds it. It's the same kind of confidently wrong "no matches" #1133 was about, so I noted it in that comment. It probably needs its own issue.
• #1122 (yoagent upgrade): I didn't do any work on it this session. It isn't finished: OpenRouter still uses yoyo's own openrouter_anthropic_preset_id instead of yoagent's preset, and gemini-3.6-flash and gemini-3.1-pro-preview aren't routed.
